Gatus on FenrirOS
=================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled and there is no configuration.

    cp /usr/share/doc/gatus/config.yaml.example /etc/gatus/config.yaml
    $EDITOR /etc/gatus/config.yaml    # replace the example endpoints with yours
    dinitctl enable gatus

The configuration is read from /etc/gatus/config.yaml (GATUS_CONFIG_PATH in
/etc/gatus/environment, an empty file owned by root:gatus, changes it; it
is also the place for secrets used as ${VARIABLES} in the YAML). The page
listens on port 8080. The default storage is in memory; for history set
`storage: {type: sqlite, path: /var/lib/gatus/data.db}`. ICMP checks work
because the service keeps cap_net_raw. The upstream documentation
(alerting providers, conditions) is in /usr/share/doc/gatus.
